  "def-nagata-blowup-product-domination-maps",
  "def-nagata-composition-of-blowups-comparison",
  "def-nagata-effective-cartier-ideal",
  "def-nagata-extended-ideal",
  "def-nagata-global-blowup",
  "def-nagata-invertible-ideal",
  "def-nagata-proj-closed-center-finite-degree"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Put $X_1=\\operatorname{Bl}_{\\mathcal I}(X)$ and\n$\\mathcal J'=\\mathcal J\\mathcal O_{X_1}$. By the extended-ideal equality,\n$\\mathcal J'=\\mathcal I_E^d\\mathcal I_{Z'}$. The product-ideal comparison\n[thm-nagata-blowup-product-ideal] therefore gives an isomorphism over\n$X$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{Bl}_{\\mathcal J'}(X_1)\n\\xrightarrow{\\sim}\\operatorname{Bl}_{\\mathcal I\\mathcal J}(X).\n$$",
   "uses": [
    "thm-nagata-blowup-product-ideal"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "Since $\\mathcal I_E^d$ is invertible, the invertible-factor comparison\n[lemma-nagata-blowup-invertible-factor] gives a canonical isomorphism\n$\\operatorname{Bl}_{\\mathcal I_{Z'}}(X_1)\\cong \\operatorname{Bl}_{\\mathcal J'}(X_1)$. Their composite is the map\n$\\Omega_{Z,Z'}$ in the definition; the reverse composite of the inverse\ncomparisons is the stated reverse map.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-blowup-invertible-factor"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "For completeness, these maps are the universal lifts for the same quotient:\non the iterated blow-up the product of the tautological invertible quotients\nis the tautological quotient of $\\mathcal I\\mathcal J$, while on the\n$\\mathcal I\\mathcal J$-blow-up its two factor quotients give the tautological\nquotients for $\\mathcal I$ and for $\\mathcal J'$; multiplying by the inverse\nof the local generator of $\\mathcal I_E^d$ gives the quotient for\n$\\mathcal I_{Z'}$. Thus each composite is an $X$-morphism inducing the\noriginal tautological quotient. Uniqueness in the blow-up universal\nproperty, first over $X$ and then over $X_1$, makes both composites identities.\nThe center ideal $\\mathcal K=\\mathcal I\\mathcal J$ is finite type, hence\ndefines a finite-presentation closed immersion, and\n[lemma-nagata-composition-center-ideal] gives its support as\n$|V(\\mathcal I)|\\cup b(|Z'|)$.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-composition-center-ideal"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
